From a1bae60ae0af59447ed078c4af0537db5082bf80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:12:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] DecodeComponent: set FLAG_DROP_FRAME on kAborted so skipped
 works complete
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The kAborted arm of onDecodeDone() masked output.flags with
FLAG_DROP_FRAME instead of setting it. That is dead code in the flush
flow (reportAbandonedWorks sweeps those works wholesale), but a decoder
that completes a mid-stream skipped frame through kAborted — a P/B frame
whose references never entered the DPB — left the work with no flag, no
output, and isWorkDone() forever false: it head-of-line-blocked
pumpReportWork() and input stalled at the pipeline depth (~28 works)
before the next keyframe could arrive.

Setting the flag makes isWorkDone() pass immediately;
reportWorkIfFinished() already clears it before reporting so the
framework sees a plain no-output work and regains pipeline capacity.

Change-Id: Ib1ca8f59be38d865c82eab8b9ae3e4018a5b31b8
---
 components/DecodeComponent.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/DecodeComponent.cpp b/components/DecodeComponent.cpp
index 0476307..dabd2e7 100644
--- a/components/DecodeComponent.cpp
+++ b/components/DecodeComponent.cpp
@@ -485,8 +485,14 @@ void DecodeComponent::onDecodeDone(int32_t bitstreamId, VideoDecoder::DecodeStat
     switch (status) {
     case VideoDecoder::DecodeStatus::kAborted:
         work->input.buffers.front().reset();
+        // SET the drop flag rather than masking with it: a decoder that skips a
+        // frame mid-stream (missing references) completes the work through this
+        // path, and without the flag isWorkDone() never passes — the work then
+        // head-of-line-blocks pumpReportWork() and input stalls at the pipeline
+        // depth. reportWorkIfFinished() clears the flag again before reporting,
+        // so the framework sees a plain no-output work and regains capacity.
         work->worklets.front()->output.flags = static_cast<C2FrameData::flags_t>(
-                work->worklets.front()->output.flags & C2FrameData::FLAG_DROP_FRAME);
+                work->worklets.front()->output.flags | C2FrameData::FLAG_DROP_FRAME);
         mOutputBitstreamIds.push(bitstreamId);
 
         pumpReportWork();
-- 
2.54.0

